{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":57433,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"fc702ada-82ab-5c2d-b6b4-52b07f309a9a","total_cost_usd":0.48099300000000006,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10177,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5458,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10177,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5458,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10177,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10177},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4433,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004533000000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5458,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10177,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.47646000000000005,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-i1-reviewer-fable-40\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:125813c0f228fcecd435\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"All 20 values in the declared independent-unit column bee_id (OB-01 through OB-20) are distinct, and all 20 arena_id values are likewise distinct; no independent unit contributes more than one row to the binomial test.\",\"observed_value\":{\"n_rows\":20,\"n_unique_bee_id\":20,\"n_unique_arena_id\":20},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":21,\"quoted_text\":\"bee_id,arena_id,intertegular_span_mm,latency_min,first_choice\\nOB-01,ARN-101,2.1,7.4,uv_marked\\n...\\nOB-20,ARN-120,2.3,8.1,uv_marked\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow actively guards against repeated-unit entry: check_one_row_per_bee raises a ValueError if any bee_id or arena_id occurs more than once, and this check runs before the binomial test.\",\"observed_value\":\"duplicate bee_id or arena_id would abort the analysis\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":36,\"end_line\":44,\"quoted_text\":\"def check_one_row_per_bee(trials):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Confirm no bee and no arena contributes more than a single row.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    bees = [row[\\\"bee_id\\\"] for row in trials]\\n    arenas = [row[\\\"arena_id\\\"] for row in trials]\\n    if len(set(bees)) != len(bees):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"a bee_id occurs twice: rows would not be independent\\\")\\n    if len(set(arenas)) != len(arenas):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"an arena_id occurs twice: rows would not be independent\\\")\\n    return len(set(bees)), len(set(arenas))\"}]},{\"description\":\"The data description states each row is one bee tested once, no bee was retested and no arena reused, and names bee_id as the independent-unit column; the file's structure matches this claim exactly.\",\"observed_value\":\"one row per independent unit, as described\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":9,\"end_line\":13,\"quoted_text\":\"No bee was tested twice and no arena was\\nreused, so the file has exactly as many data lines as there were bees.\\n\\nOne row is: one wild-caught female mason bee tested once in her own two-tube choice arena\\nIndependent unit column: bee_id\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result was independently recomputed and matches: 15 of 20 uv_marked first choices (rows OB-04, OB-08, OB-13, OB-17, OB-19 are plain), and the exact two-sided binomial p-value for 15/20 against 0.5 is 21700/1048576 * 2 = 0.041389, exactly as reported.\",\"observed_value\":{\"marked\":15,\"plain\":5,\"recomputed_p_two_sided\":0.041389},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":25,\"end_line\":28,\"quoted_text\":\"- Observed proportion choosing the UV-marked tube: 0.750\\n- Two-sided exact p-value: 0.041389\\n\\n[selected-result] Exact two-sided binomial test on 20 independent females: 15 of 20 (0.750) landed first on the UV-marked tube, p = 0.041389 against a null proportion of 0.5, rejecting indifference at the 5% level.\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The only dependence-adjacent design feature found: arenas were run sequentially over two weeks with left/right tube placement alternated across arenas, a shared procedural factor across rows. This is a between-arena design consideration, not a repeated entry of any independent unit, so it does not instantiate the target issue class.\",\"observed_value\":\"shared design factor only; no unit repetition\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":3,\"end_line\":7,\"quoted_text\":\"Over two weeks of late spring, twenty wild-caught female mason bees (*Osmia\\nbicornis*) were released one at a time into a private mesh arena. Each arena\\nheld two otherwise identical nesting tubes: one whose entrance rim carried a\\nUV-reflective paint mark, and one left plain, with the left/right placement\\nalternated from arena to arena.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by searching for any repeated independent-unit entry: I enumerated all 20 bee_id values (OB-01..OB-20) and all 20 arena_id values (ARN-101..ARN-120) in data/input.csv and confirmed every value is unique, so no bee or arena contributes multiple rows to the row-independent binomial procedure. I checked whether the workflow could silently aggregate or duplicate rows before testing; instead it enforces uniqueness (check_one_row_per_bee) and would raise on any duplicate. I also verified the report's claims are not merely asserted but reproducible from the data: recounting first_choice gives 15 uv_marked / 5 plain, the mean intertegular span is 46.8/20 = 2.34 mm, and the exact two-sided binomial p-value 2*P(X>=15 | n=20, p=0.5) = 43400/1048576 = 0.041389 matches the reported value. No path to the target issue class survived these checks.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-i1-reviewer-fable-40","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:125813c0f228fcecd435","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"All 20 values in the declared independent-unit column bee_id (OB-01 through OB-20) are distinct, and all 20 arena_id values are likewise distinct; no independent unit contributes more than one row to the binomial test.","observed_value":{"n_rows":20,"n_unique_bee_id":20,"n_unique_arena_id":20},"source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":21,"quoted_text":"bee_id,arena_id,intertegular_span_mm,latency_min,first_choice\nOB-01,ARN-101,2.1,7.4,uv_marked\n...\nOB-20,ARN-120,2.3,8.1,uv_marked"}]},{"description":"The workflow actively guards against repeated-unit entry: check_one_row_per_bee raises a ValueError if any bee_id or arena_id occurs more than once, and this check runs before the binomial test.","observed_value":"duplicate bee_id or arena_id would abort the analysis","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":36,"end_line":44,"quoted_text":"def check_one_row_per_bee(trials):\n    \"\"\"Confirm no bee and no arena contributes more than a single row.\"\"\"\n    bees = [row[\"bee_id\"] for row in trials]\n    arenas = [row[\"arena_id\"] for row in trials]\n    if len(set(bees)) != len(bees):\n        raise ValueError(\"a bee_id occurs twice: rows would not be independent\")\n    if len(set(arenas)) != len(arenas):\n        raise ValueError(\"an arena_id occurs twice: rows would not be independent\")\n    return len(set(bees)), len(set(arenas))"}]},{"description":"The data description states each row is one bee tested once, no bee was retested and no arena reused, and names bee_id as the independent-unit column; the file's structure matches this claim exactly.","observed_value":"one row per independent unit, as described","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":9,"end_line":13,"quoted_text":"No bee was tested twice and no arena was\nreused, so the file has exactly as many data lines as there were bees.\n\nOne row is: one wild-caught female mason bee tested once in her own two-tube choice arena\nIndependent unit column: bee_id"}]},{"description":"The selected result was independently recomputed and matches: 15 of 20 uv_marked first choices (rows OB-04, OB-08, OB-13, OB-17, OB-19 are plain), and the exact two-sided binomial p-value for 15/20 against 0.5 is 21700/1048576 * 2 = 0.041389, exactly as reported.","observed_value":{"marked":15,"plain":5,"recomputed_p_two_sided":0.041389},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":25,"end_line":28,"quoted_text":"- Observed proportion choosing the UV-marked tube: 0.750\n- Two-sided exact p-value: 0.041389\n\n[selected-result] Exact two-sided binomial test on 20 independent females: 15 of 20 (0.750) landed first on the UV-marked tube, p = 0.041389 against a null proportion of 0.5, rejecting indifference at the 5% level."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The only dependence-adjacent design feature found: arenas were run sequentially over two weeks with left/right tube placement alternated across arenas, a shared procedural factor across rows. This is a between-arena design consideration, not a repeated entry of any independent unit, so it does not instantiate the target issue class.","observed_value":"shared design factor only; no unit repetition","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":3,"end_line":7,"quoted_text":"Over two weeks of late spring, twenty wild-caught female mason bees (*Osmia\nbicornis*) were released one at a time into a private mesh arena. Each arena\nheld two otherwise identical nesting tubes: one whose entrance rim carried a\nUV-reflective paint mark, and one left plain, with the left/right placement\nalternated from arena to arena."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by searching for any repeated independent-unit entry: I enumerated all 20 bee_id values (OB-01..OB-20) and all 20 arena_id values (ARN-101..ARN-120) in data/input.csv and confirmed every value is unique, so no bee or arena contributes multiple rows to the row-independent binomial procedure. I checked whether the workflow could silently aggregate or duplicate rows before testing; instead it enforces uniqueness (check_one_row_per_bee) and would raise on any duplicate. I also verified the report's claims are not merely asserted but reproducible from the data: recounting first_choice gives 15 uv_marked / 5 plain, the mean intertegular span is 46.8/20 = 2.34 mm, and the exact two-sided binomial p-value 2*P(X>=15 | n=20, p=0.5) = 43400/1048576 = 0.041389 matches the reported value. No path to the target issue class survived these checks.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":32419,"ttft_stream_ms":2462,"time_to_request_ms":11,"type":"result","duration_ms":57630,"uuid":"c52b509f-64be-4166-8613-25f562547d3c"}
